## Item 5 — can `f7b10b5` be the `--reviewed-commit`?

**L_simple launch (launcher closure): yes, and it is the earliest commit that can be.** The launcher closure changed at `34a076a` (this review's scope: `tools/exp04_launcher.py`, `tools/exp05_gates.py`; every other launcher-closure file is at its `f19b9b6` blob), so `build_fields` refuses `--reviewed-commit f19b9b6` from the current tree (`launcher closure differs from reviewed commit`), and `f7b10b5` is clean (`closure_record` at `f7b10b5`: no blob difference, no later commit) — provided no commit between now and the launch touches any of the 12 launcher-closure or 11 training-closure files and the tree is clean outside `worklog/` at launch (`git log f7b10b5..HEAD -- train_xRIR_backbone.py tools/exp04_launcher.py tools/exp04_launch.sh tools/exp04_probe.py tools/exp05_params.py tools/exp05_gates.py tools/exp05_probe.py tools/provenance.py tools/yaw_aug.py tools/yaw_rotation.py model/ utils/ treble_multi_room_dataset/` must be empty immediately before). **Consequence: L_simple needs a new fit/timing probe at the launch commit.** The existing receipt `ckpt/exp05/L_simple/_probe_20260913T102644_L_simple.json` is bound to `f19b9b6` in both the receipt and its probe attempt's manifest; the new validator refuses it at `f7b10b5` (verified on the real file). The probe must run on the launch GPU with no co-tenant (else `PROBE_NOT_CLEAN`), i.e. on GPU 0 after exp_04's evaluation chain, as the notebook already schedules; its `--reviewed-commit` must equal the `full` launch's. `tools/exp04_launcher.py` must not change between that probe and `full`. Changes since `f19b9b6` in this closure and their review status: `34a076a` — reviewed here (approve with changes, no blocker). If nit 1 (message split) is taken, it touches `tools/exp05_gates.py` and moves the launch commit again; take it before the L_simple probe or after all trainings, not between.

**exp_05 evaluations (evaluator/writer closures): yes.** `tools.exp05_eval` (`a2ffbb38…`, 16 files) and `tools.exp04_eval_launch` (`15f9c984…`, 15 files) have no file changed since `f19b9b6`; any commit from `f19b9b6` to `f7b10b5` (and later ones that leave those files alone) is a valid `--reviewed-commit` for the 60 k = 0 runs, the six yaw blocks and the M re-evaluation through `--tier M`. The pins `closures.evaluator = a2ffbb38…` / `closures.writer = 15f9c984…` are as recorded in the round-2 close-out's observation 6; `closures.training_launcher` for the four S/L arms must be a single digest, which requires **all four** `final/train_manifest.json` files to carry the same launcher digest — S_simple, S_cylindrical and L_cylindrical were launched at `f19b9b6` (`0bff0d4f…`), (verified read-only: `ckpt/exp05/{S_simple/attempt_20260913T123905,S_cylindrical/attempt_20260914T000333,L_cylindrical/attempt_20260914T120322}/train_manifest.json` all record `source_closures.launcher.sha256 = 0bff0d4fe270…`, training `5b2da2504e22…`), so an L_simple trained at `f7b10b5` (`efde5a31…`) **would be refused by the producer's `training launcher closure` check** (`param_curve.py:216-217`, plan §10a A8 "the four new arms' training-launcher closure digests equal each other and the approved pin"). This is a plan-level consequence of polishing the launcher between launches, not a code defect; it needs a Planner decision before the L_simple launch: (a) an amendment reading A8's "equal each other" as "each equal to a reviewed launcher digest" with the pin becoming a set/list (small producer change, re-review), or (b) launching L_simple from a checkout whose 12 launcher-closure files are at the `f19b9b6` blobs (i.e. reverting `34a076a`'s two files before the launch and re-applying after — the running L_cylindrical is unaffected either way), or (c) accepting that the exp_05 curve is analysed only after a policy amendment. The notebook's 14:05 note ("L_simple's `--reviewed-commit` will be the round-4 close-out commit") does not yet address this.

**Producer (`tools.param_curve` closure `b6a99f67…`):** changed since `f19b9b6` by `1ec0457` + `d1f0d61` (round-3 close-out review: approve with changes, no blocker; its finding 1 is closed by `f7b10b5`) and `f7b10b5` (this review). `closures.producer_param_curve` is computed at the fill commit; nit 2 (one line in `tools/param_curve.py`) moves it, so land it before `approved_digests.json` is filled.

## Verdict

**Approve with changes.** Blocking findings: **none.** Non-blocking: nits 1–3 (message split for the commit-mismatch case, file-name tie on the training bindings, inert pre-seed in `test_full_cli_uses_receipt_projection`) may be batched with the next touch of the respective file. The open item before L_simple's launch is the A8 single-digest consequence in Item 5 (a Planner/plan decision, not a Coder fix).
